From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add /targetpet to target your own pet

Add a /targetpet command that targets the player's own pet, so it can be bound
to a hotkey or a social button instead of clicking the pet window.

The pet's spawn id is ActorInfo->PetID (a SHORT that holds -1, not 0, when
there is no pet), looked up with get_entity_by_id() and targeted with
set_target(). With no pet the command prints "You do not have a pet to
target."; if the id is not in the spawn table (zoning, out of range) it prints
"Your pet could not be found (out of range or zoning).". Either way the current
target is left alone. A charmed pet fills the same field, so it works there too.

A small class registers the command, wired the same way as the other
single-purpose features. Documented in the README.
---
